  "description": "Mistral Large 4 (aka ML4 / Le Chonk) is Mistral AI's flagship open-weight, general-purpose multimodal Mixture-of-Experts model, unifying instruction following, reasoning, coding, and agentic workflows in a single set of weights. Mistral's Hugging Face card describes it as a 1T-parameter model with 49B active parameters per token (52B including embeddings and output layers; docs list 1.05T total with a 1.6B vision encoder), 128 routed experts (4 active) plus 1 shared expert, a 1M-token context window, text+image input and text output, and three reasoning efforts (low, medium, high default). It entered public preview on 2026-10-06; on 2026-10-29 Mistral released the weights of an improved, further-RL-trained version (same API id mistral-large-4) under the Mistral Ecosystem Open-Weight License (modified MIT; Model-as-a-Service businesses need a separate commercial license), priced at $0.70/$0.07/$2.10 per million input/cached input/output tokens.",
